# Source PDFs under pdfs/ ARE committed — via git-LFS (project Decision 2).
# See .gitattributes. So do NOT blanket-ignore *.pdf. Ignore only stray PDFs
# that land outside the tracked pdfs/ tree.
*.pdf
!pdfs/
!pdfs/**
# Phase D — DORIS GPP dual-provenance copies + parked pre-1974 volumes under
# sources/gpp/ are also committed via git-LFS (.gitattributes: sources/**/*.pdf).
!sources/
!sources/**
# The tiny offline parse-pipeline test fixtures ARE committed (regenerate with
# tests/fixtures/generate_fixtures.py) — the suite needs them.
!tests/fixtures/*.pdf

# Legacy local raw-harvest staging (pre-Decision-2 layout), if ever created.
data/raw/

# Regenerated harvest outputs — produced fresh by each (dry-)run, not source of truth.
# The committed dataset (when we publish one) will be a deliberate snapshot, not these.
index/
manifest.csv
gaps.md

# The publishable corpus (corpus/) is committed as of 2026-07-13 — it is the
# § 3-113.1 deliverable, a deliberate snapshot regenerable by scripts/run_parse.py.
# Plain-text Markdown + JSON (diffable, greppable on GitHub); NOT LFS.
# (index/textlayer_report.json stays ignored via the index/ rule above — it's a
# probe artifact, not part of the published dataset.)

# Python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Scratch output from scripts/run_volume_ocr.py -- rendered page PNGs + model
# output, regenerated per run, not source of truth. The per-page JSON that
# Phase E actually consumes is published separately, and committed, under
# sources/gpp/volumes/ocr/ (see scripts/run_volume_ocr.py).
#
# vlm-ocr-runs/post1974/ is the scratch half of the same split for the post-1974
# scans: scripts/run_post1974_ocr.py renders there and commits its page records
# to sources/ocr/<year>/<eo_id>/ instead. It also PRUNES this directory as it
# goes (--keep-renders, default `flagged`), because 1,799 pages of renders plus
# overlays is 2-5 GB and only the flagged documents are worth opening.
vlm-ocr-runs/

# Picture-element crops from scripts/run_picture_clips.py -- city seals, mayoral
# signatures and the odd figure, cut out of the volume PDFs. Lossless 300 dpi
# PNGs, 472 MB of them, cheaply regenerable from the committed page JSON under
# sources/gpp/volumes/ocr/ plus the LFS'd volume PDFs. Source of truth, and
# still not committed -- same rule as the rendered pages above.
#
# What IS committed is the web derivative under vlm-pics-web/: the same crops at
# JPEG q85, 53 MB, written by scripts/build_web_crops.py. The public explorer
# serves those out of its own GitHub Pages build, which is the one thing the
# PNGs cannot do -- Pages does not resolve LFS pointers, and 472 MB would not
# fit under its 1 GB site cap regardless. Plain git rather than LFS,
# deliberately, so that build can check this repo out without `lfs: true` and
# spend no LFS bandwidth on images.
vlm-pics/

# Per-volume run transcripts from run_full_vlm_pre_1974.sh, and per-worker ones
# from scripts/run_post1974_ocr.py under vlm-logs/post1974/. Console output of a
# reproducible local job -- keep them to debug a run, not to share one.
vlm-logs/

# Scratch from the (now superseded) dots.ocr/MLX prototype under experiments/.
experiments/dots-ocr-mlx/runs/

# Single-page / short-range extracts cut out of the bound volumes while
# developing the OCR pipeline. `!sources/**` above un-ignores everything under
# sources/, and .gitattributes would push these through git-LFS, so without this
# rule a stray `git add sources/` commits prototype scratch as LFS objects.
# The 14 real volumes have no `_page` suffix and are unaffected.
sources/gpp/volumes/*_page*.pdf

# Node (if an MCP server is added later)
node_modules/
dist/
dist-static/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log

# Per-run state for run_full_vlm_post_1974.sh: the step logs it mirrors off the
# rented GPU box, the phase ledger, the droplet id it must be able to destroy,
# and a run-scoped known_hosts. Scratch, not source of truth.
.post1974-run/

# for viewing md
.obsidian/
